        "procedure": "Er(NO3)3·5H2O (89 mg, 0.2 mmol) dissolved in MeOH (10 mL) was mixed with H2salen in MeCN (10 mL). NEt3 (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) was added, and the solution was heated at 70 °C for 2 h. The mixture was filtered, slowly evaporated in the dark, and dried in air. Yield 35%. Lattice water content was checked by TGA (dehydration complete at 110 °C). Elemental analysis calcd for C96H110Er4N12O25: C 46.10, H 4.43, N 6.72; found C 45.85, H 4.29, N 7.16. No separate mass of H2salen is stated.",
